{
  "name": "orb",
  "description": "In-house catch orb (original design): a glossy teal-to-indigo sphere lit from the upper left, with a cyan rim, inside a free gold C (the Conductor C) that stands face-on round it with a pixel of floor between, open on the right, its upper end a latch with a glint. The ring never touches the sphere; no band across it, no button, no red. Each row is a string, one palette key per pixel; '_' is transparent. Every frame is 16x16, centred on the same point and resting on the ground by its bottom row. 'closed' waits, is thrown and is flown as a message; 'spinDown', 'spinLeft' and 'spinUp' are the C turned a quarter at a time (closed, spinDown, spinLeft, spinUp is the ring spinning clockwise); 'open' is the closed orb with a slit of light rising from the lower left through its centre to the latch side, where it spills out through the C's opening.",
